      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Given that $n\\ge 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(n+1)!}{(n-1)!}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n(n+1)!=(n+1)\\cdot n\\cdot (n-1)!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $(n-1)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n+1)!}{(n-1)!} & =\\frac{(n+1)\\cdot n\\cdot (n-1)!}{(n-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(n+1)\\cdot n\\cdot \\cancel{(n-1)!}}{\\cancel{(n-1)!}} \\\\  & =n(n+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
